WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.101
-Wow!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:05.472
How exciting is this?!

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:07.706
Hello.

00:00:07.706 --> 00:00:09.876
So, here is a little bit of fun

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:12.678
for you to have
at the airport, okay?

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:14.947
Little prank for you to play.

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:18.852
All you need to do is go down
to your local fancy dress shop,

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:22.856
hire yourself a pilot's outfit,
pop it on,

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:25.158
then head down
to your local airport,

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:28.795
sit in the bar,
and get completely wasted.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.563
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:34.467
Just watch people around you
losing their minds.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.902
"Hey, where are you going?

00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:39.005
Ooh! That's my one!

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:41.374
Don't worry.
I know a shortcut."

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:48.681
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:49.816
I'm a nervous flyer.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.417
I get very nervous when I fly.

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:53.085
And they don't do enough
to help us, do they?

00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:56.255
The safety demonstration --
can we drop that already?

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:58.158
It's 2017.

00:00:58.158 --> 00:01:00.960
We've got
the seat-belt fastening down.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.162
We don't need any of it.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.096
Why do we have to start
every flight

00:01:04.096 --> 00:01:06.299
with a cabin crew
performing a little play

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:09.835
entitled "The Horrific Ways You
Could Die on this Aircraft"?

00:01:09.835 --> 00:01:12.171
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:15.074
It's...

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.377
It's 'cause we have
this routine on planes,

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:20.579
and we're used to the routine,
so no one questions the routine.

00:01:20.579 --> 00:01:23.816
Well, I'm the guy
who questions the routine.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:24.850
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.052
I was on a plane the other day.

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.520
I was doing something
we have all done

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.954
loads of times before
on the plane --

00:01:28.954 --> 00:01:32.058
lifting up the blind
for takeoff and landing.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.226
For the first time ever,

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:35.828
I decided
I would ask the stewardess

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:40.500
why I had to lift up the blind
for takeoff and landing.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.570
It is a question
that I regret asking...

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:44.603
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:46.072
...'cause this is
the genuine reason.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:47.540
I said, "Madam, out of interest,

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.676
why do I have to lift up the
blind for takeoff and landing?"

00:01:50.676 --> 00:01:52.712
She looked at me.
Do you know what she said?

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.714
She went, "Well, sir,
if something were

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:59.619
to go wrong with the engine,
then you are the pilot's eyes."

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:02.455
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:04.223
"I beg your pardon!"

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:05.491
[ Laughter continues ]

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:08.727
"I'm not ready for
that level of responsibility,

00:02:08.727 --> 00:02:11.631
and no one told me that
when I purchased the ticket.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:12.931
I was very much led to believe

00:02:12.931 --> 00:02:14.933
I was traveling
in the capacity of passenger,

00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:16.102
not bloody co-pilot!"

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:17.403
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:20.506
"Also, I think you may have
picked the wrong guy.

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:21.841
Let's look at the evidence here.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.177
I've had a sleeping pill,
two glasses of red wine,

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:27.346
and I just cried whilst watching
'Inside Out.'

00:02:27.346 --> 00:02:28.414
I'm not your man!"

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.049
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:32.485
How does this --

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:35.421
How does this scenario
play out in your head?

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:38.091
As we're nose-diving
towards the ground,

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:39.492
and I look out of the window

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.660
and see smoke billowing
from the engine,

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:44.196
I'm meant to, what --
just amble up to the cockpit,

00:02:44.196 --> 00:02:46.566
pop my head through the door,
"Awfully sorry, gents.

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.534
Your eyes in the back here.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.670
I don't know
whether you're aware of this,

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.904
but one of the wings
has fallen off."

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:52.905
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:54.273
"You might want to buckle up.

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:56.109
I will send someone through
to show you how it's done.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.376
Thank you!"

00:02:57.376 --> 00:02:59.145
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:00.913
It's crazy!

00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:05.952
[ Cheering continues ]

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.086
That very much made it sound

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:08.454
like I said something
to the stewardess.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:10.423
Obviously,
I didn't actually complain.

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:11.457
I'm British.

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:12.659
I wouldn't dream
of causing a fuss.

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:13.826
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:15.394
I don't think
I'm capable of complaining.

00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:16.662
I hate complaining.

00:03:16.662 --> 00:03:18.231
If I'm with someone
that's complaining in, say,

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:21.200
a restaurant, I die inside.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.768
I'm like, "Just, please,
don't say anything.

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:24.337
Just don't make a scene.

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:25.838
Just eat the nut, all right?

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:28.540
We have an EpiPen at home.
We will deal with it later.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:29.775
What? No!
Everything's wonderful!

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:31.210
Thank you.
No, no! She loves it, as well.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.378
Her neck is always that big.
That's normal. Thank you."

00:03:33.378 --> 00:03:39.218
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:41.353
Social anxiety --
that's my problem.

00:03:41.353 --> 00:03:42.788
I have social anxiety.

00:03:42.788 --> 00:03:44.189
That's why, hands down,

00:03:44.189 --> 00:03:46.926
the hardest bit of traveling
for me -- Passport Control.

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.895
Oh, I hate Passport Control.

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:50.629
I cannot deal
with being questioned

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:52.198
by a figure of authority.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.199
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:55.367
Every time, I fall apart --

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:58.804
under the most basic
of questioning, as well.

00:03:58.804 --> 00:04:00.039
I walk up, they're like,

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:01.807
"Where are you
traveling from today, sir?"

00:04:01.807 --> 00:04:03.376
"France.
No, Spain -- Italy!

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:04.810
Damn it!
Sorry, England.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.546
Don't know why I said that,
didn't sleep on the plane.

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:07.546
Drugs didn't work.

00:04:07.546 --> 00:04:08.781
Not drugs like 'drugs' drugs!

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.549
I mean,
drugs like sleeping-pill drugs.

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:12.351
I don't have any drugs on me.
I'm not a mule.

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:13.685
Please don't look in my bottom.

00:04:13.685 --> 00:04:16.022
I have explosive diarrhea.
Not explosive like a bomb!

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:17.790
Oh! I just said 'bomb'
in an airport!

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.858
No! It's not a --
It's a phrase!

00:04:19.858 --> 00:04:21.227
I keep saying 'bomb'!

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:22.528
Bomb, bomb, bomb!

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.364
The more you say it,
the less offensive it becomes!

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:25.998
Bomb, bomb, bomb!
Ooh! It's like a song!

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:27.699
I'll stop saying 'bomb' now
'cause you're all looking at me

00:04:27.699 --> 00:04:28.734
like I'm a terrorist.

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:30.436
I promise you,
I'm not a terrorist!

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:31.904
I'm just Jack, plain old Jack.

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.573
Hi, Jack!
Not 'hijack'!

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.007
[Bleep] No!
Don't shoot!"

00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:37.776
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:04:37.776 --> 00:04:40.246
Thank you very much!

